This is a simple, clearly visible and independent existence; 
here the knights, and very much later the peasants too, are and 
remain in a certain sense always the lords of their land.

But they visit them only in passing; 
there is no room here, no interest and often no means to feed 
and pay a player for any length of time.

What this 
class is struggling with the princes for, and what it finally attains, 
is not the destruction of monopoly rule.

Conversely, for Philip Augustus the 
victory in the foreign war strengthens his power within his 
dominion. ;

He added—to mention only his major acquisi- 
tions—Normandy, then one of the largest and richest territories 
in the whole realm; the regions of Anjou, Maine and Touraine; 
important parts of Poitou and Saintonge;

There is no one to contest it with 
him and in 1363 he gives it to his youngest son Philip, whom he 
particularly loves;

Then 
their life, their social existence, their striving attains fulfilment; 
they seize the contested opportunities.

Its western boundaries are the Channel and the Atlantic; 
the whole coastal area as far down as Navarre is now in the 
hands of the French kings.

Within 
this balanced apparatus enormous forces are latent but bound; 
without someone to release them they can have no effect.

The youth of the aristocracy is without hope; 
the unrest and social pressure emanating from these displaced 
people is felt everywhere in the life of this society.

